# Landfall — runtime external-binary contract
#
# Every external binary the SERVER spawns at runtime (Process.start / Process.run
# / the ProcessStarter `_start` alias in server/landfall_server/lib) MUST be
# declared here. `deploy/pi-gen/preflight.sh` scans the server source and FAILS
# the build if it finds a spawned binary that is not listed below.
#
# This exists because a binary added in code but never provisioned in the image
# (avahi-publish, May 2026) crash-looped the server and trapped the Pi on the
# boot splash. Declaring provisioning here forces that decision to be explicit
# and reviewed.
#
# Format (whitespace-separated):
#   <binary>  <provided-by>  <reason...>
#
# <provided-by> is one of:
#   image:<apk-package>  Installed in server/landfall_server/Dockerfile via
#                        `apk add <apk-package>`. preflight verifies the
#                        Dockerfile actually installs that package.
#   host:<note>          Provided by the Raspberry Pi host, NOT the container.
#                        Only valid if the container does not depend on it at
#                        runtime (e.g. the call path is disabled in the image).
#   dev:<note>           Used only in local/dev runs, never in the Pi image.

avahi-publish  host:avahi-utils  Pi host avahi-daemon publishes _landfall._tcp; container broadcast disabled via LANDFALL_MDNS_BROADCAST=false, and start() is crash-safe if the binary is absent.
dns-sd         dev:macos         macOS-only mDNS CLI for desktop dev runs; never invoked in the Linux container.
